   "line": [
    "Bd6"
   ],
   "spoken": "The bishop to d6 almost hands the piece back and hands us a big lead in development, because it blocks in his other bishop. The tactical idea is to trade twice on e5, then f4 to shove the bishop back, then e5 — though it doesn't quite win a piece because of a bishop check on c5 and a knight jump to e4. So keeping the tension with the bishop to g5 is the sober alternative.",
